exports[`docs generate should render level.md 1`] = `
[
  "<!-- This file is generated by \`xrf-cli docs generate\`. Do not edit manually. -->",
  "",
  "# Level commands",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR: commands -->",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli level albedo\`",
  "",
  "Report how the base textures of a level's lit surfaces sit as albedo, against the range real materials span",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli level albedo [OPTIONS] <path|--root <root>>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` |  |  | Path to a compiled level directory, the one holding \`level\` and \`level.geom\` |",
  "| \`-r, --root <root>...\` |  |  | Root holding an installation's levels. Repeat to layer roots, highest priority first |",
  "| \`-l, --level <level>\` |  |  | Name of the level to read from the mounted roots, as \`levels\` knows it |",
  "| \`--source <source>\` |  | \`auto\` | How to read the path: auto treats it as an installation only when it declares one, directory ignores any declaration, volumes mounts every archive volume beneath it, installation requires one, containing-installation searches parent directories for one. Possible values: \`auto\`, \`directory\`, \`volumes\`, \`installation\`, \`containing-installation\`. |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli level build\`",
  "",
  "Build an SDK Level Editor scene into a level directory, as the editor's Build writes it. From the scene's parts it writes level.game, level.env_mod and level.fog_vol, and level.spawn, level_rs.spawn, level.ps_static, level.snd_static, level.snd_env and level.wallmarks where the scene holds them. Given --game-materials it also writes what level compile reads, from the scene's objects: build.prj with the scene's build options, level.ltx, level.hom and level.som where objects occlude, build.details and its atlas build_details.dds where the scene holds details, build.aimap where it holds an AI map, the impostor atlas level_lods.dds and level_lods_nm.dds where a multi-use object has an impostor, and each breakable part as meshes/brkbl#<n>.ogf",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli level build [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the scene's .level; its parts are read from the directory beside it named after it |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Path of the level directory to write the files into |",
  "| \`--objects <objects>...\` |  |  | Objects root ($objects$) the scene's objects are read from, repeatable, each object from the first root holding it; by default the objects directory beside the scene's levels directory, where level decompile writes them |",
  "| \`--textures <textures>\` |  |  | Textures root ($game_textures$) the detail objects' textures are merged from into build_details.dds, and the multi-use objects' impostor strips (lod/lod_&lt;object&gt;.dds and _nm) into level_lods.dds and level_lods_nm.dds; by default gamedata/textures beside the scene's rawdata directory, where level decompile writes them |",
  "| \`--game-materials <game-materials>\` |  |  | Game material library, gamemtl.xr, the objects' surfaces name their game materials from; with it, the build writes build.prj, level.ltx and the occluders |",
  "| \`--sdk-impostor-atlas\` |  |  | Keep the impostor atlas within SDK 0.7's 2048 by 2048, refusing a level of more than 128 impostors as that Level Editor does; by default it grows to 4096 a side, as Anomaly's largest levels ship it |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Overwrite the files the build writes where the directory already holds them, and remove those of its own an earlier build wrote that this one does not; without it, a directory holding one is refused before the scene is read |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli level compile\`",
  "",
  "Compile a level directory that level build wrote into the files the game loads. The steps run in this process, in order: geometry (level, level.geom, level.geomx and level.cform, as xrLC builds them, and the build.cform and build.lights the later steps read), light (the light of the vertices, lightmaps and terrain, baked in the same pass as the geometry, so it runs only with geometry; without it the level gets flat neutral light), details (level.details lit from build.details, as xrDO_Light lights it) and ai (level.ai from build.aimap, as xrAI -f compiles it, then checked as a graph). Before any step runs, the compile checks that every input of the chosen steps is there, and a .thm for every texture build.prj names",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli level compile [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the level directory, &lt;levels&gt;/&lt;level&gt;, that level build wrote into |",
  "| \`--steps <steps>\` |  |  | Steps to run, comma-separated; they always run in the order geometry, light, details, ai. Every step by default; light runs only with geometry. Possible values: \`geometry\`, \`light\`, \`details\`, \`ai\`. Accepts multiple values separated by \`,\`. |",
  "| \`--gamedata <gamedata>\` |  |  | Game data directory to read gamemtl.xr, shaders_xrlc.xr and the textures from; by default the gamedata directory holding the level's levels directory |",
  "| \`--textures <textures>...\` |  |  | Textures root searched for the .thm of every texture build.prj names, and the image of each texture with alpha, before the game data's textures directory, which is always read last; repeatable, each file taken from the first root holding it |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Overwrite what the steps write where the level directory already holds it (the geometry's files and lightmap pages, level.details, level.ai), and remove the lightmap pages of an earlier compile past this one's; without it, a directory holding one is refused before any step runs. A replaced level.ai keeps its identity while its graph is unchanged, so the level's spawn still loads |",
  "| \`--backend <backend>\` |  | \`auto\` | What traces the rays of the light, details and ai steps: auto uses the GPU where it supports ray tracing, else the CPU; gpu uses the GPU only, on D3D12 where dxc/dxcompiler.dll is beside the CLI, else on Vulkan; cpu uses the CPU, the reference result. Possible values: \`cpu\`, \`gpu\`, \`auto\`. |",
  "| \`--ai-covers <ai-covers>\` |  | \`full\` | Covers the ai step computes: full traces them against build.cform, as xrAI -f does; none sets every cover to 0, as xrAI -draft does, and needs no build.cform, for a map to walk before the geometry is compiled. Possible values: \`none\`, \`full\`. |",
  "| \`--quality <quality>\` |  | \`scene\` | How finely the light step lights the level: scene uses build.prj's own sky, sun, lightmap density and samples; draft is a quick estimate, regenerating the sky and sun (also those written to build.lights) at quality 1, lighting lightmaps at 3 texels a metre with one sample each, and each multi-use object, such as a tree, from one sample. Possible values: \`scene\`, \`draft\`. |",
  "| \`-j, --jobs <JOBS>\` |  | \`auto\` | How much of the machine to use: 'auto', a worker count, or a share such as '50%' |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli level decompile\`",
  "",
  "Decompile a compiled level's directory into an SDK Level Editor scene (.level and its parts), with a .level.xrf.json provenance sidecar beside it. The scene holds the parts the build passes through (particles, sounds, sound environments, fog volumes, wall marks, patrol paths, respawn points, environment modifiers and entity spawns), the level's glows and lights, and its static geometry as one .object per sector with the sectors and portals",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli level decompile [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the level's directory, holding level, build.lights, level.game, level.ps_static and the rest |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Path of the .level to write; its parts go in the directory beside it named after it, its sidecar beside it, and its name is the level's |",
  "| \`--objects <objects>\` |  |  | Objects root ($objects$) the scene's .object files are written under, at levels/&lt;level&gt;/; by default the objects directory beside the destination's directory, as the SDK lays out rawdata/levels and rawdata/objects |",
  "| \`--textures <textures>\` |  |  | Game textures root ($game_textures$) the textures the objects need for the build, such as the tree models' impostor strips under lod/, are written under; by default gamedata/textures beside the destination's rawdata directory, as the SDK lays out editors/rawdata and editors/gamedata |",
  "| \`--surfaces <surfaces>\` |  | \`infer\` | How the geometry's surfaces are dressed: infer each game material from the collision face beneath and a compiler shader fitting what the level shows, or give every surface the editor's defaults. Possible values: \`infer\`, \`defaults\`. |",
  "| \`--game-materials <game-materials>\` |  |  | Game material library naming the collision materials; gamemtl.xr in the level's gamedata by default |",
  "| \`--compiler-shaders <compiler-shaders>\` |  |  | Compiler shader library inferred compiler shaders are chosen from; shaders_xrlc.xr in the level's gamedata by default |",
  "| \`--library <library>...\` |  |  | Object library root, such as an SDK's rawdata/objects: its objects found placed in the static geometry and its trees found as tree models are placed by reference and copied beside the objects, the level's detail models are looked up among its objects, and its surfaces' pairings of engine and compiler shaders break ties between compiler shaders that fit; repeatable |",
  "| \`--spawn <spawn>\` |  |  | Root spawn whose objects on the level replace level.spawn's entities, read from spawns/&lt;spawn&gt;.spawn beside the level's levels directory; all.spawn by default where it exists |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Overwrite an existing .level, its parts, its sidecar, its objects and textures, and remove the parts and objects of the level's own an earlier decompile wrote that this one does not; without it, the scene or the level's objects already there are refused before the level is read |",
  "| \`--refuse-links\` |  |  | Refuse to write through links or junctions already below the destination, instead of following them |",
  "| \`-j, --jobs <JOBS>\` |  | \`auto\` | How much of the machine to use: 'auto', a worker count, or a share such as '50%' |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli level info\`",
  "",
  "Print what a compiled level holds",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli level info [OPTIONS] <path|--root <root>>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` |  |  | Path to a compiled level directory, the one holding \`level\` and \`level.geom\` |",
  "| \`-r, --root <root>...\` |  |  | Root holding an installation's levels. Repeat to layer roots, highest priority first |",
  "| \`-l, --level <level>\` |  |  | Name of the level to read from the mounted roots, as \`levels\` knows it |",
  "| \`--source <source>\` |  | \`auto\` | How to read the path: auto treats it as an installation only when it declares one, directory ignores any declaration, volumes mounts every archive volume beneath it, installation requires one, containing-installation searches parent directories for one. Possible values: \`auto\`, \`directory\`, \`volumes\`, \`installation\`, \`containing-installation\`. |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli level materials\`",
  "",
  "Report the game materials each of a level's render surfaces lies on, read off its collision form",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli level materials [OPTIONS] <path|--root <root>>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` |  |  | Path to a compiled level directory, the one holding \`level\` and \`level.geom\` |",
  "| \`-r, --root <root>...\` |  |  | Root holding an installation's levels. Repeat to layer roots, highest priority first |",
  "| \`-l, --level <level>\` |  |  | Name of the level to read from the mounted roots, as \`levels\` knows it |",
  "| \`--source <source>\` |  | \`auto\` | How to read the path: auto treats it as an installation only when it declares one, directory ignores any declaration, volumes mounts every archive volume beneath it, installation requires one, containing-installation searches parent directories for one. Possible values: \`auto\`, \`directory\`, \`volumes\`, \`installation\`, \`containing-installation\`. |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli level verify\`",
  "",
  "Verify that a compiled level's geometry can be drawn the way the renderer addresses it, and that its AI map is a graph the engine can walk",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli level verify [OPTIONS] <path|--root <root>>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` |  |  | Path to a compiled level directory, the one holding \`level\` and \`level.geom\` |",
  "| \`-r, --root <root>...\` |  |  | Root holding an installation's levels. Repeat to layer roots, highest priority first |",
  "| \`-l, --level <level>\` |  |  | Name of the level to read from the mounted roots, as \`levels\` knows it |",
  "| \`--source <source>\` |  | \`auto\` | How to read the path: auto treats it as an installation only when it declares one, directory ignores any declaration, volumes mounts every archive volume beneath it, installation requires one, containing-installation searches parent directories for one. Possible values: \`auto\`, \`directory\`, \`volumes\`, \`installation\`, \`containing-installation\`. |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

exports[`docs generate should render ltx.md 1`] = `
[
  "<!-- This file is generated by \`xrf-cli docs generate\`. Do not edit manually. -->",
  "",
  "# LTX commands",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR: commands -->",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ltx find\`",
  "",
  "Find where a section or field is written, declared or patched, across every config a project holds. A config that does not parse is reported as not searched, and the run fails, since it may hold the answer",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ltx find [OPTIONS] <--section <section>|--field <field>|--value <value>> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to a folder with ltx files, or to a game installation root holding fsgame.ltx (fsgame_&lt;game&gt;.ltx in an Enhanced Edition) |",
  "| \`--section <section>\` |  |  | Section to find, without brackets or operation prefix. Matches the whole name in any case, as the engine lowercases section names |",
  "| \`--field <field>\` |  |  | Field to find, without operation prefix. Matches the whole name, case-sensitively |",
  "| \`--value <value>\` |  |  | Text a written value must contain, case-sensitively |",
  "| \`--dltx\` |  |  | Resolve configs with the Monolith/Anomaly DLTX patch dialect, applying mod_&lt;base&gt;_*.ltx files |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ltx format\`",
  "",
  "Format LTX and INI files",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ltx format [OPTIONS] <path>...",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Ltx files, or folders holding them |",
  "| \`-c, --check\` |  |  | Run formatter in check mode |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ltx inspect\`",
  "",
  "Explain one resolved section: its fields, and where each value is written",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ltx inspect [OPTIONS] --section <section> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to a folder with ltx files, or to a game installation root holding fsgame.ltx (fsgame_&lt;game&gt;.ltx in an Enhanced Edition) |",
  "| \`--section <section>\` | yes |  | Name of the section to explain, without its brackets |",
  "| \`-e, --entry <entry>\` |  |  | Entry point to resolve, when more than one declares the section |",
  "| \`--dltx\` |  |  | Resolve configs with the Monolith/Anomaly DLTX patch dialect, applying mod_&lt;base&gt;_*.ltx files |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ltx list\`",
  "",
  "List the LTX configs a project holds, and the role each one plays",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ltx list [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to a folder with ltx files, or to a game installation root holding fsgame.ltx (fsgame_&lt;game&gt;.ltx in an Enhanced Edition) |",
  "| \`--dltx\` |  |  | Resolve configs with the Monolith/Anomaly DLTX patch dialect, applying mod_&lt;base&gt;_*.ltx files |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ltx verify\`",
  "",
  "Verify LTX and INI configs",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ltx verify [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to a folder with ltx files, or to a game installation root holding fsgame.ltx (fsgame_&lt;game&gt;.ltx in an Enhanced Edition) |",
  "| \`--dltx\` |  |  | Resolve configs with the Monolith/Anomaly DLTX patch dialect, applying mod_&lt;base&gt;_*.ltx files |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

exports[`docs generate should render object.md 1`] = `
[
  "<!-- This file is generated by \`xrf-cli docs generate\`. Do not edit manually. -->",
  "",
  "# Object commands",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR: commands -->",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli object compile\`",
  "",
  "Compile an SDK .object into the OGF the engine loads (a skeleton with bones, else a static visual), or into a .dm detail model where the destination is one",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli object compile [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the .object to compile |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Path of the OGF to write, or of a .dm, whose flags and scale range come from the sidecar of an object decompiled from one and are the editor's defaults otherwise |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Overwrite an existing OGF |",
  "| \`--tangents <tangents>\` |  | \`auto\` | Tangent method of a skeleton: auto follows the provenance sidecar beside a decompiled object (MikkTSpace for a model exported from Blender) and the Actor Editor's otherwise; actor-editor or mikktspace forces one. A static visual stores no tangents. Possible values: \`auto\`, \`actor-editor\`, \`mikktspace\`. |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli object decompile\`",
  "",
  "Decompile a skeleton or static OGF, or a .dm detail model, into an SDK .object, with a .object.xrf.json provenance sidecar beside it",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli object decompile [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the OGF or .dm to decompile |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Path of the .object to write; its sidecar is written beside it |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Overwrite an existing .object and sidecar |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli object verify\`",
  "",
  "Compile an SDK .object in memory and compare it with the OGF it should stand in for",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli object verify [OPTIONS] --ogf <ogf> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the .object to compile |",
  "| \`--ogf <ogf>\` | yes |  | Path to the OGF the compile should stand in for, such as the one the object was exported to |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

exports[`docs generate should render ogf.md 1`] = `
[
  "<!-- This file is generated by \`xrf-cli docs generate\`. Do not edit manually. -->",
  "",
  "# OGF commands",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR: commands -->",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ogf fix\`",
  "",
  "Rewrite OGF visuals into well-formed bytes, changing nothing the engine reads",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ogf fix [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to an ogf file or a directory to sweep |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` |  |  | Path to the resulting ogf file, defaults to in place rewrite of the source file; not for a directory |",
  "| \`--dry-run\` |  |  | Report what would change and how many bytes would go without writing any file |",
  "| \`-j, --jobs <JOBS>\` |  | \`auto\` | How much of the machine to use: 'auto', a worker count, or a share such as '50%' |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ogf info\`",
  "",
  "Print what an OGF visual holds",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ogf info [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the OGF file |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ogf patch-motion-refs\`",
  "",
  "Rewrite the motion refs of an OGF visual",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ogf patch-motion-refs [OPTIONS] --refs <refs> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to ogf file |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` |  |  | Path to resulting ogf file, defaults to in place rewrite of the source file |",
  "| \`--refs <refs>...\` | yes |  | Motion ref to store in the ogf file. Repeat to store several, in order |",
  "| \`--dry-run\` |  |  | Validate the rewrite and report the result without writing any file |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ogf patch-texture-refs\`",
  "",
  "Rename a texture reference of an OGF visual",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ogf patch-texture-refs [OPTIONS] --from <from> --to <to> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to ogf file |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` |  |  | Path to resulting ogf file, defaults to in place rewrite of the source file |",
  "| \`--from <from>\` | yes |  | Texture reference to rename, matched exactly |",
  "| \`--to <to>\` | yes |  | Texture reference to write in its place |",
  "| \`--dry-run\` |  |  | Validate the change and report the result without writing any file |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli ogf verify\`",
  "",
  "Verify that OGF visuals can be packed for rendering",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli ogf verify [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to an ogf file or a directory to sweep |",
  "| \`--root <root>...\` |  |  | Additional root searched for textures after the visual's own tree, repeatable |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

