  "| \`--keep-prefix <keep-prefix>...\` |  |  | Keep motions whose name starts with this prefix. Repeat to keep several |",
  "| \`--dry-run\` |  |  | Validate the change and report the result without writing any file |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli omf info\`",
  "",
  "Print what an OMF file holds",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli omf info [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the OMF file |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli omf rename-motions\`",
  "",
  "Rename the motions of an OMF file",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli omf rename-motions [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> --map <map> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to omf file |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Path to resulting omf file |",
  "| \`-m, --map <map>\` | yes |  | Path to JSON object mapping existing motion names to new ones |",
  "| \`--strict\` |  |  | Require every motion in the file to be covered by the map |",
  "| \`--dry-run\` |  |  | Validate the change and report the result without writing any file |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli omf repack\`",
  "",
  "Repack an OMF file, or verify that OMF files repack into the bytes they were read from",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli omf repack [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Omf file to repack, or with --verify an omf file or a directory of them |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` |  |  | Repacked omf file written |",
  "| \`--verify\` |  |  | Verify that repacked bytes match the source instead of writing them |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

exports[`docs generate should render particle.md 1`] = `
[
  "<!-- This file is generated by \`xrf-cli docs generate\`. Do not edit manually. -->",
  "",
  "# Particle commands",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR: commands -->",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli particle find\`",
  "",
  "Find the effects drawing with a texture or shader or running an action, and the groups playing an effect",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli particle find [OPTIONS] <--texture <texture>|--shader <shader>|--action <action>|--effect <effect>> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the particle library, particles.xr |",
  "| \`--texture <texture>...\` |  |  | Texture to find the effects sampling, with or without its extension. Repeat to find several |",
  "| \`--shader <shader>...\` |  |  | Shader to find the effects drawing with, such as particles\\add. Repeat to find several |",
  "| \`--action <action>...\` |  |  | Action type to find the effects running, as the unpacked library names it, such as TargetColor. Repeat to find several |",
  "| \`--effect <effect>...\` |  |  | Effect to find the groups playing or spawning it. Repeat to find several |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli particle info\`",
  "",
  "Print what a particle file holds",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli particle info [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the particle library, particles.xr |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli particle inspect\`",
  "",
  "Explain one effect or group: its sprite, frames and actions, or the effects it plays and spawns",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli particle inspect [OPTIONS] --name <name> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the particle library, particles.xr |",
  "| \`--name <name>\` | yes |  | Name of the effect or group, in any case and with either slash, such as explosions\\campfire |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli particle list\`",
  "",
  "List the effects and groups a particle library holds, with what each draws and plays",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli particle list [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the particle library, particles.xr |",
  "| \`--kind <kind>\` |  |  | List only effects or only groups. Possible values: \`effect\`, \`group\`. |",
  "| \`--name <name>\` |  |  | List only names containing this text, in any case and with either slash, such as campfire or explosions\\effects |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli particle pack\`",
  "",
  "Pack an unpacked particles file folder into one particles.xr",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli particle pack [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Unpacked particles file folder |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Packed particles.xr written |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace the destination when it is already there, once the new one is ready |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli particle repack\`",
  "",
  "Read a particles.xr and write it packed again",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli particle repack [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Packed particles.xr |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Repacked particles.xr written |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace the destination when it is already there, once the new one is ready |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli particle re-unpack\`",
  "",
  "Read an unpacked particles file folder and write it unpacked again",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli particle re-unpack [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Unpacked particles file folder |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Folder the re-unpacked particles file is written to |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace the destination when it is already there, once the new one is ready |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli particle unpack\`",
  "",
  "Unpack a particles.xr into a folder of text files",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli particle unpack [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Packed particles.xr |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Folder the unpacked particles file is written to |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace the destination when it is already there, once the new one is ready |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli particle verify\`",
  "",
  "Verify that a particles.xr reads",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli particle verify [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Packed particles.xr, or its unpacked folder with --unpacked |",
  "| \`-u, --unpacked\` |  |  | Read the path as an unpacked particles file folder |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

exports[`docs generate should render spawn.md 1`] = `
[
  "<!-- This file is generated by \`xrf-cli docs generate\`. Do not edit manually. -->",
  "",
  "# Spawn commands",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR: commands -->",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli spawn build\`",
  "",
  "Build a root spawn from a gamedata root's levels, as SDK 0.7's xrAI -s does: each level's level.ai, level.spawn and level.game into one spawn with the game graph, its cross tables, the entities, artefact points and patrols. The same levels give the same file",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli spawn build [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Gamedata root holding configs/game_levels.ltx, and by default the levels' directories under levels/ and the spawn written under spawns/ |",
  "| \`--levels-root <levels-root>\` |  |  | Directory holding the levels' directories; by default levels/ under the gamedata root |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` |  |  | The .spawn file to write; by default spawns/all.spawn under the gamedata root, the game's own |",
  "| \`--levels <levels>...\` |  |  | Levels to build, by directory name, comma-separated or repeated; by default every level the game lists whose directory holds level.ai, level.spawn and level.game. Accepts multiple values separated by \`,\`. |",
  "| \`--start <start>\` |  |  | Level the actor starts on, where it is not the actor's own: it moves to that level's first game vertex |",
  "| \`--strict-separators\` |  |  | Refuse the build where a restrictor flagged for the separator check cuts an AI map apart, rather than report it |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Overwrite the spawn where its directory already holds it, the name compared without case |",
  "| \`-j, --jobs <JOBS>\` |  | \`auto\` | How much of the machine to use: 'auto', a worker count, or a share such as '50%' |",
  "| \`--dltx\` |  |  | Resolve configs with the Monolith/Anomaly DLTX patch dialect, applying mod_&lt;base&gt;_*.ltx files |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli spawn info\`",
  "",
  "Print what a spawn file holds",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli spawn info [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to a root spawn such as all.spawn, or to a level's level.spawn |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli spawn pack\`",
  "",
  "Pack an unpacked spawn file folder into one *.spawn",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli spawn pack [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Unpacked spawn file folder |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Packed *.spawn written |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace the destination when it is already there, once the new one is ready |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli spawn repack\`",
  "",
  "Read a *.spawn and write it packed again",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli spawn repack [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Packed *.spawn |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Repacked *.spawn written |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace the destination when it is already there, once the new one is ready |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli spawn re-unpack\`",
  "",
  "Read an unpacked spawn file folder and write it unpacked again",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli spawn re-unpack [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Unpacked spawn file folder |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Folder the re-unpacked spawn file is written to |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace the destination when it is already there, once the new one is ready |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli spawn unpack\`",
  "",
  "Unpack a *.spawn into a folder of text files",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli spawn unpack [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Packed *.spawn |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Folder the unpacked spawn file is written to |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace the destination when it is already there, once the new one is ready |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli spawn verify\`",
  "",
  "Verify that a *.spawn reads",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli spawn verify [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Packed *.spawn, or its unpacked folder with --unpacked |",
  "| \`-u, --unpacked\` |  |  | Read the path as an unpacked spawn file folder |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

exports[`docs generate should render sprite.md 1`] = `
[
  "<!-- This file is generated by \`xrf-cli docs generate\`. Do not edit manually. -->",
  "",
  "# Sprite commands",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR: commands -->",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli sprite pack-description\`",
  "",
  "Pack the sprites a texture description xml declares into its sheets",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli sprite pack-description [OPTIONS] --base <base> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | XML file describing the sheets |",
  "| \`--base <base>\` | yes |  | Folder the described sprites are read from |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` |  |  | Folder the packed sheets are written to, defaults to the base folder |",
  "| \`--file <file>...\` |  |  | Name of a described file to pack, repeatable; packs every described file if omitted |",
  "| \`--strict\` |  |  | Fail on a sprite that cannot be read instead of leaving its place empty |",
  "| \`--refuse-links\` |  |  | Refuse to write through links or junctions already below the destination, instead of following them |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli sprite pack-equipment\`",
  "",
  "Pack an equipment sprite from separate icon files",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli sprite pack-equipment [OPTIONS] --system-ltx <system-ltx> --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Folder holding one icon per section |",
  "| \`--system-ltx <system-ltx>\` | yes |  | Path to system ltx file or root folder with ltx files |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Equipment sprite dds file to write |",
  "| \`--gamedata <gamedata>\` |  |  | Path to gamedata folder for resources usage |",
  "| \`--strict\` |  |  | Fail on an icon that cannot be read or placed instead of skipping it |",
  "| \`--dltx\` |  |  | Resolve configs with the Monolith/Anomaly DLTX patch dialect, applying mod_&lt;base&gt;_*.ltx files |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli sprite unpack-description\`",
  "",
  "Unpack the sprites a texture description xml declares out of its sheets",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli sprite unpack-description [OPTIONS] --base <base> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | XML file describing the sheets |",
  "| \`--base <base>\` | yes |  | Folder the described sheets are read from |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` |  |  | Folder the sprites are written to, defaults to the base folder |",
  "| \`--file <file>...\` |  |  | Name of a described file to unpack, repeatable; unpacks every described file if omitted |",
  "| \`--strict\` |  |  | Fail on a sheet that cannot be read or a sprite outside its sheet instead of skipping it |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Overwrite sprites already in the destination, names compared without case; without it, one there is refused before any sprite is cut |",
  "| \`-j, --jobs <JOBS>\` |  | \`auto\` | How much of the machine to use: 'auto', a worker count, or a share such as '50%' |",
  "| \`--refuse-links\` |  |  | Refuse to write through links or junctions already below the destination, instead of following them |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli sprite unpack-equipment\`",
  "",
  "Unpack separate icon files out of an equipment sprite",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli sprite unpack-equipment [OPTIONS] --system-ltx <system-ltx> --dest <dest> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Equipment sprite dds file to read |",
  "| \`--system-ltx <system-ltx>\` | yes |  | Path to system ltx file or root folder with ltx files |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Folder the section icons are written to |",
  "| \`--dltx\` |  |  | Resolve configs with the Monolith/Anomaly DLTX patch dialect, applying mod_&lt;base&gt;_*.ltx files |",
  "| \`--refuse-links\` |  |  | Refuse to write through links or junctions already below the destination, instead of following them |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli sprite verify-equipment\`",
  "",
  "Check an equipment sprite's inventory icon grid rects for overlaps",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli sprite verify-equipment [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | System ltx file, or a root folder of ltx files |",
  "| \`--dltx\` |  |  | Resolve configs with the Monolith/Anomaly DLTX patch dialect, applying mod_&lt;base&gt;_*.ltx files |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

exports[`docs generate should render thm.md 1`] = `
[
  "<!-- This file is generated by \`xrf-cli docs generate\`. Do not edit manually. -->",
  "",
  "# THM commands",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR: commands -->",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli thm bump-alignment\`",
  "",
  "Report whether each texture's bump belongs to its diffuse, by how closely the bump's slopes follow the diffuse's edges",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli thm bump-alignment [OPTIONS] <path>...",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Root holding the textures and their descriptors. Give several to layer them, highest priority first |",
  "| \`--source <source>\` |  | \`containing-installation\` | How to read the path: auto treats it as an installation only when it declares one, directory ignores any declaration, volumes mounts every archive volume beneath it, installation requires one, containing-installation searches parent directories for one. Possible values: \`auto\`, \`directory\`, \`volumes\`, \`installation\`, \`containing-installation\`. |",
  "| \`--prefix <prefix>\` |  |  | Limit to the descriptors of one logical subtree, such as textures\\wpn |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli thm info\`",
  "",
  "Print what a THM file holds, every field of a texture descriptor by the SDK's own names",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli thm info [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to thm file |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli thm patch-bump\`",
  "",
  "Repoint the bump texture reference of a THM file",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli thm patch-bump [OPTIONS] <--to <to>|--off> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to thm file |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` |  |  | Path to resulting thm file, defaults to in place rewrite of the source file |",
  "| \`--to <to>\` |  |  | Bump texture reference to write, engine style without extension, for example 'wpn\\wpn_pm\\wpn_pm_bump' |",
  "| \`--off\` |  |  | Declare no bump at all, clearing the mode and the name; use for a bump that does not exist and is not going to |",
  "| \`--dry-run\` |  |  | Validate the change and report the result without writing any file |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli thm set-field\`",
  "",
  "Set named fields on texture descriptors in place, every other byte of each left as it was; a directory sets them on every texture descriptor below it",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli thm set-field [OPTIONS] <--texture-type <texture-type>|--format <format>|--mip-filter <mip-filter>|--bump-mode <bump-mode>|--bump-name <bump-name>|--detail-name <detail-name>|--detail-scale <detail-scale>|--material <material>|--material-weight <material-weight>|--border-color <border-color>|--fade-color <fade-color>|--fade-amount <fade-amount>|--fade-delay <fade-delay>|--ext-normal-map <ext-normal-map>|--virtual-height <virtual-height>|--set-flag <set-flag>|--clear-flag <clear-flag>> <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to a thm file, or to a directory whose texture descriptors are all edited |",
  "| \`--dry-run\` |  |  | Report which descriptors would change without writing any |",
  "| \`--texture-type <texture-type>\` |  |  | Texture type, the gate the engine reads first. Possible values: \`image\`, \`cube-map\`, \`bump-map\`, \`normal-map\`, \`terrain\`. |",
  "| \`--format <format>\` |  |  | Format the converter builds the texture in. Possible values: \`dxt1\`, \`dxt1-alpha\`, \`dxt3\`, \`dxt5\`, \`rgba4444\`, \`rgba1555\`, \`rgb565\`, \`rgb\`, \`rgba\`, \`nvhs\`, \`nvhu\`, \`a8\`, \`l8\`, \`a8l8\`. |",
  "| \`--mip-filter <mip-filter>\` |  |  | Filter the converter reduces each mip level with; 'advanced' selects the SDK's own chain. Possible values: \`advanced\`, \`point\`, \`box\`, \`triangle\`, \`quadratic\`, \`cubic\`, \`catrom\`, \`mitchell\`, \`gaussian\`, \`sinc\`, \`bessel\`, \`hanning\`, \`hamming\`, \`blackman\`, \`kaiser\`. |",
  "| \`--bump-mode <bump-mode>\` |  |  | Whether the renderer binds the bump pair. Possible values: \`none\`, \`use\`, \`use-parallax\`. |",
  "| \`--bump-name <bump-name>\` |  |  | Bump texture, engine style without extension, for example 'wpn\\wpn_pm\\wpn_pm_bump' |",
  "| \`--detail-name <detail-name>\` |  |  | Detail texture, engine style without extension; empty for none |",
  "| \`--detail-scale <detail-scale>\` |  |  | How many times the detail texture repeats over the texture |",
  "| \`--material <material>\` |  |  | Shading pair the renderer blends between. Possible values: \`oren-nayar-blin\`, \`blin-phong\`, \`phong-metal\`, \`metal-oren-nayar\`. |",
  "| \`--material-weight <material-weight>\` |  |  | Where between the two shadings the texture sits |",
  "| \`--border-color <border-color>\` |  |  | Border colour, AARRGGBB in hex |",
  "| \`--fade-color <fade-color>\` |  |  | Colour the mip chain fades towards, AARRGGBB in hex; its alpha is the alpha fade's target |",
  "| \`--fade-amount <fade-amount>\` |  |  | Percent of the way each faded mip level moves towards the fade colour |",
  "| \`--fade-delay <fade-delay>\` |  |  | First mip level the fade reaches |",
  "| \`--ext-normal-map <ext-normal-map>\` |  |  | Normal map the bump generator takes instead of deriving one, engine style; empty for none |",
  "| \`--virtual-height <virtual-height>\` |  |  | Relief height the bump generator reads, and nothing at runtime |",
  "| \`--set-flag <set-flag>...\` |  |  | Flag to set, by its SDK name; repeat or separate with commas. Possible values: \`flGenerateMipMaps\`, \`flBinaryAlpha\`, \`flAlphaBorder\`, \`flColorBorder\`, \`flFadeToColor\`, \`flFadeToAlpha\`, \`flDitherColor\`, \`flDitherEachMIPLevel\`, \`flDiffuseDetail\`, \`flImplicitLighted\`, \`flHasAlpha\`, \`flBumpDetail\`. Accepts multiple values separated by \`,\`. |",
  "| \`--clear-flag <clear-flag>...\` |  |  | Flag to clear, by its SDK name; repeat or separate with commas. Possible values: \`flGenerateMipMaps\`, \`flBinaryAlpha\`, \`flAlphaBorder\`, \`flColorBorder\`, \`flFadeToColor\`, \`flFadeToAlpha\`, \`flDitherColor\`, \`flDitherEachMIPLevel\`, \`flDiffuseDetail\`, \`flImplicitLighted\`, \`flHasAlpha\`, \`flBumpDetail\`. Accepts multiple values separated by \`,\`. |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli thm write\`",
  "",
  "Write a complete texture descriptor for a DDS file, at the SDK's new-file defaults with the size and format the file states, then the fields named",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli thm write [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to the dds file to write a descriptor for |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` |  |  | Path of the thm file to write, defaults to the one beside the dds file |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace the thm file where it already exists; without it, one there is refused before reading |",
  "| \`--dry-run\` |  |  | Report the descriptor without writing it |",
  "| \`--texture-type <texture-type>\` |  |  | Texture type, the gate the engine reads first. Possible values: \`image\`, \`cube-map\`, \`bump-map\`, \`normal-map\`, \`terrain\`. |",
  "| \`--format <format>\` |  |  | Format the converter builds the texture in. Possible values: \`dxt1\`, \`dxt1-alpha\`, \`dxt3\`, \`dxt5\`, \`rgba4444\`, \`rgba1555\`, \`rgb565\`, \`rgb\`, \`rgba\`, \`nvhs\`, \`nvhu\`, \`a8\`, \`l8\`, \`a8l8\`. |",
  "| \`--mip-filter <mip-filter>\` |  |  | Filter the converter reduces each mip level with; 'advanced' selects the SDK's own chain. Possible values: \`advanced\`, \`point\`, \`box\`, \`triangle\`, \`quadratic\`, \`cubic\`, \`catrom\`, \`mitchell\`, \`gaussian\`, \`sinc\`, \`bessel\`, \`hanning\`, \`hamming\`, \`blackman\`, \`kaiser\`. |",
  "| \`--bump-mode <bump-mode>\` |  |  | Whether the renderer binds the bump pair. Possible values: \`none\`, \`use\`, \`use-parallax\`. |",
  "| \`--bump-name <bump-name>\` |  |  | Bump texture, engine style without extension, for example 'wpn\\wpn_pm\\wpn_pm_bump' |",
  "| \`--detail-name <detail-name>\` |  |  | Detail texture, engine style without extension; empty for none |",
  "| \`--detail-scale <detail-scale>\` |  |  | How many times the detail texture repeats over the texture |",
  "| \`--material <material>\` |  |  | Shading pair the renderer blends between. Possible values: \`oren-nayar-blin\`, \`blin-phong\`, \`phong-metal\`, \`metal-oren-nayar\`. |",
  "| \`--material-weight <material-weight>\` |  |  | Where between the two shadings the texture sits |",
  "| \`--border-color <border-color>\` |  |  | Border colour, AARRGGBB in hex |",
  "| \`--fade-color <fade-color>\` |  |  | Colour the mip chain fades towards, AARRGGBB in hex; its alpha is the alpha fade's target |",
  "| \`--fade-amount <fade-amount>\` |  |  | Percent of the way each faded mip level moves towards the fade colour |",
  "| \`--fade-delay <fade-delay>\` |  |  | First mip level the fade reaches |",
  "| \`--ext-normal-map <ext-normal-map>\` |  |  | Normal map the bump generator takes instead of deriving one, engine style; empty for none |",
  "| \`--virtual-height <virtual-height>\` |  |  | Relief height the bump generator reads, and nothing at runtime |",
  "| \`--set-flag <set-flag>...\` |  |  | Flag to set, by its SDK name; repeat or separate with commas. Possible values: \`flGenerateMipMaps\`, \`flBinaryAlpha\`, \`flAlphaBorder\`, \`flColorBorder\`, \`flFadeToColor\`, \`flFadeToAlpha\`, \`flDitherColor\`, \`flDitherEachMIPLevel\`, \`flDiffuseDetail\`, \`flImplicitLighted\`, \`flHasAlpha\`, \`flBumpDetail\`. Accepts multiple values separated by \`,\`. |",
  "| \`--clear-flag <clear-flag>...\` |  |  | Flag to clear, by its SDK name; repeat or separate with commas. Possible values: \`flGenerateMipMaps\`, \`flBinaryAlpha\`, \`flAlphaBorder\`, \`flColorBorder\`, \`flFadeToColor\`, \`flFadeToAlpha\`, \`flDitherColor\`, \`flDitherEachMIPLevel\`, \`flDiffuseDetail\`, \`flImplicitLighted\`, \`flHasAlpha\`, \`flBumpDetail\`. Accepts multiple values separated by \`,\`. |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

exports[`docs generate should render translation.md 1`] = `
[
  "<!-- This file is generated by \`xrf-cli docs generate\`. Do not edit manually. -->",
  "",
  "# Translation commands",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR: commands -->",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli translation build\`",
  "",
  "Build translation files into gamedata",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli translation build [OPTIONS] --dest <dest> <path>...",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Root holding translation sources, or one source file. Give several to layer them, highest priority first |",
  "| \`--source <source>\` |  | \`containing-installation\` | How to read the path: auto treats it as an installation only when it declares one, directory ignores any declaration, volumes mounts every archive volume beneath it, installation requires one, containing-installation searches parent directories for one. Possible values: \`auto\`, \`directory\`, \`volumes\`, \`installation\`, \`containing-installation\`. |",
  "| \`--prefix <prefix>\` |  |  | Limit to one logical subtree, such as translations |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Directory the built string tables are written to |",
  "| \`-l, --language <language>\` |  | \`all\` | Language to build, or all of them |",
  "| \`--no-sort\` |  |  | Preserve source order instead of sorting dynamic translation files |",
  "| \`--refuse-links\` |  |  | Refuse to write through links or junctions already below the destination, instead of following them |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli translation format\`",
  "",
  "Normalize JSON translation sources",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli translation format [OPTIONS] <path>...",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Json translation sources, or folders holding them |",
  "| \`-c, --check\` |  |  | Run formatter in check mode |",
  "| \`--line-endings <line-endings>\` |  |  | Write these line endings instead of preserving each file's own, and judge them in check mode. Possible values: \`lf\`, \`crlf\`. |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli translation initialize\`",
  "",
  "Initialize translation files",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli translation initialize [OPTIONS] <path>",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Path to translation folder |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli translation parse\`",
  "",
  "Parse XML translations into JSON sources",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli translation parse [OPTIONS] --language <language> --dest <dest> <path>...",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Root holding raw xml translations. Give several to layer them, highest priority first |",
  "| \`--source <source>\` |  | \`containing-installation\` | How to read the path: auto treats it as an installation only when it declares one, directory ignores any declaration, volumes mounts every archive volume beneath it, installation requires one, containing-installation searches parent directories for one. Possible values: \`auto\`, \`directory\`, \`volumes\`, \`installation\`, \`containing-installation\`. |",
  "| \`--prefix <prefix>\` |  |  | Limit to one logical subtree, such as configs\\text\\eng |",
  "| \`-l, --language <language>\` | yes |  | Language every entry read by this run is filed under. Raw xml carries no language, so it is declared rather than guessed |",
  "| \`-d, --dest <dest>\` | yes |  | Directory the json sources are written to, merging with any already there |",
  "| \`--file <file>\` |  |  | Restrict the run to one string table, by file name |",
  "| \`-f, --force\` |  |  | Replace existing text that differs, instead of keeping what is already there |",
  "| \`--dry-run\` |  |  | Report what would be written without writing it |",
  "| \`--strict\` |  |  | Answer with a check failure when anything was unreadable or off schema |",
  "| \`--refuse-links\` |  |  | Refuse to write through links or junctions already below the destination, instead of following them |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "## \`xrf-cli translation verify\`",
  "",
  "Verify that translation sources build to tables the game loads as written, and are translated into every language",
  "",
  "\`\`\`txt",
  "xrf-cli translation verify [OPTIONS] <path>...",
  "\`\`\`",
  "",
  "| Option | Required | Default | Description |",
  "| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------- |",
  "| \`<path>\` | yes |  | Root holding translation sources, or one source file. Give several to layer them, highest priority first |",
  "| \`--source <source>\` |  | \`containing-installation\` | How to read the path: auto treats it as an installation only when it declares one, directory ignores any declaration, volumes mounts every archive volume beneath it, installation requires one, containing-installation searches parent directories for one. Possible values: \`auto\`, \`directory\`, \`volumes\`, \`installation\`, \`containing-installation\`. |",
  "| \`--prefix <prefix>\` |  |  | Limit to one logical subtree, such as translations |",
  "| \`-l, --language <language>\` |  | \`all\` | Language to verify, or all of them |",
  "| \`--strict\` |  |  | Also answer with a check failure when any translation is missing |",
  "| \`-s, --silent\` |  |  | Turn off logging |",
  "| \`-v, --verbose\` |  |  | Turn on verbose logging |",
  "| \`--json\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to stdout, moving human output to stderr |",
  "| \`--report <PATH>\` |  |  | Write the run's JSON report to a file |",
  "",
  "<!-- ANCHOR_END: commands -->",
]
`;

